Intelligent Street Lighting Control System

Project Description

The Intelligent Street Lighting Control System is a smart solution designed to reduce electricity consumption by automatically controlling street-light brightness based on vehicle and pedestrian movement.

The system helps save energy, improve efficiency, and support smart city development.

Features

- Automatic Street Light Control
- Manual ON/OFF Control
- Brightness Adjustment
- Vehicle Detection (Demo)
- Pedestrian Detection (Demo)
- Energy Consumption Monitoring
- Energy Saving Statistics
- Responsive Website Design

Technologies Used

- HTML – Website Structure
- CSS – Website Styling
- JavaScript – Interactive Features

Project Structure

Intelligent-Street-Lighting/
│
├── index.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
└── README.md

How to Run the Project

1. Download or extract the project folder.
2. Open the folder in Visual Studio Code.
3. Make sure all three files are in the same folder.
4. Open "index.html" in your browser.
5. You can also use the Live Server extension in VS Code.

How It Works

1. The system detects vehicle or pedestrian movement using demonstration data.
2. When movement is detected, the street light brightness increases.
3. When no movement is detected, brightness decreases.
4. Users can manually control the lights using ON/OFF buttons.
5. Energy monitoring displays estimated electricity savings.

Future Enhancements

- Real-time vehicle detection using AI.
- IoT-based street light control.
- ESP32 hardware integration.
- Live camera monitoring.
- Cloud-based energy monitoring.

Conclusion

The Intelligent Street Lighting Control System provides a simple and effective approach to reducing electricity wastage. It demonstrates how smart technology can improve street-light management and support energy-efficient smart cities.